inArmsT -- THE THREE ARMS OF opIN, EACH PINNED BY VALUE. Minted 2026-09-08 when
the groupList arm was moved to the FRONT of opIN, because until that stroke two
of these three arms had no fleet cover at all and the reorder could have broken
either one silently.

WHAT opIN DOES, and the operand order is measured, not assumed: `X IN Y` calls
opIN with `argument` = Y (the CONTAINER) and `target` = X (the NEEDLE). The arms
are tried in order and the FIRST match wins, which is the whole reason order is
load-bearing.

    IA-S1  nameSet IN "justaname"     1     the SET arm, target.isSET
    IA-S2  nameSet IN "has spaces"    0     same arm, and the discriminator
    IA-G1  TokFiles IN DesignDocs     1     the groupList arm, top level
    IA-G2  ParserGates IN DesignDocs  1     same arm, and it DESCENDS
    IA-G3  <declared field> IN ...    0     the miss control

/  EVERY ZERO ROW HAS A NON-ZERO SIBLING, and that is not decoration. A row that
only ever wants 0 cannot tell "answered false" from "answered nothing" -- the two
are identical from outside. S2 is paired with S1 and G3 with G1/G2 for exactly
that reason.

/  IA-G3 IS THE ROW THIS FILE EXISTS FOR. Before the reorder it read 1. A
registry carries BOTH a character set and a group list, so the isSET arm matched
first and `set.foundIn(target.text)` returned trueResult for EVERYTHING -- and on
a data-less field `.text` hands back the field's own tag (bear-trap 26), so a
character-set test was being fed a name. A field DECLARED in this file's own
define block, which cannot be in DesignDocs, still read HIT. Any census built on
IN was unmeasurable until this row went to 0.

/  IA-G2 IS WHY THE ARM MOVED AT ALL. Tony wanted `result = name IN field` to
search DesignDocs at any depth, which is what firstComponent gives and what plain
get does not.

/  THE FIELDS ARE WRITTEN AND READ BY ONE ACTION, DELIBERATELY. The first draft
split measure and report across two actions and every row printed a tag echo: an
undeclared name in an action body is a per-action LOCAL, so the reader saw its
own copies (bear-trap 39). Either declare them in the define block or keep them
in one action; this file keeps them in one action.
